// ============================================================================
// sync_gateway.json.template — local integration-test harness config
//
// MIRRORS: the production Sync Gateway config running on the CATALYST Lab
//   Sync Gateway VM (recorded verbatim in opserver
//   `.planning/todos/pending/verify-production-datastore-topology.md`).
//   Every value below — database name, bucket name, shared bucket access,
//   revs limit, timeouts, and the sync function itself — is the production
//   value, not a convenient default. Fidelity is the point: the failure mode
//   this harness exists to reproduce (a null `channels` array collapsing
//   document access to `[doc.owner]`) is a Sync Gateway behavior, so a stub
//   config or a mock cannot expose it.
//
// PINNED TO:
//   Sync Gateway     2.8.2-1 Community  (legacy, non-bootstrap config format)
//   Couchbase Server 6.6.0   Community
//   These two are a coherent, supported pair and match production exactly.
//   SG 3.0+ requires CBS 6.6.5+ and a different (bootstrap) config format, so
//   this file is NOT forward-compatible with an SG 3 upgrade.
//
// DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED — production `event_handlers.document_changed`:
//   Production declares four `document_changed` webhooks that POST to the
//   live CATALYST api host (filtered on doc.type for FitbitHeartRecord,
//   PhysicalActivity/FitbitRecord, Weight/FitbitWeight, and Post; the exact
//   URLs are in opserver's verify-production-datastore-topology.md). They are
//   omitted here ON PURPOSE, not by oversight: including them would make
//   every local test write attempt an outbound call to a production host, and
//   the host name is deliberately not written into this file so that a
//   copy-paste can never resurrect them. Those webhooks are Phase 10's
//   subject.
//
// ENVSUBST NOTE:
//   This file is rendered by `scripts/render_sync_gateway_config.sh`, which
//   runs `envsubst`. Every dollar-brace placeholder below is substituted from
//   `.env`. The sync function currently contains NO `$` character, so envsubst
//   cannot corrupt it. If you ever add a `$` to the JavaScript (a jQuery-style
//   identifier, a template literal), write it as a dollar-brace DOLLAR
//   placeholder — the render script exports DOLLAR='$' for exactly this,
//   following the convention established by opserver's `environment.sh`.
//   Note the render script rejects any dollar-brace sequence that survives
//   substitution, so prose in this header must not contain one either.
//
// SECRETS:
//   No credential is written here. The rendered output
//   `sync_gateway/sync_gateway.json` is gitignored; this template is tracked.
// ============================================================================
{
  "interface": ":4984",
  "adminInterface": ":4985",
  "logging": {
    "console": {
      "log_level": "info",
      "log_keys": ["HTTP", "CRUD", "Import", "Changes"]
    }
  },
  "databases": {
    "${SYNC_GATEWAY_DB}": {
      "server": "http://couchbase:8091",
      "bucket": "spring",
      "username": "${SYNC_GATEWAY_CB_USER}",
      "password": "${SYNC_GATEWAY_CB_PASSWORD}",
      "enable_shared_bucket_access": true,
      "import_docs": true,
      "allow_conflicts": false,
      "num_index_replicas": 0,
      "revs_limit": 20,
      "view_query_timeout_secs": 300,
      "users": {
        "GUEST": {
          "disabled": true,
          "admin_channels": []
        }
      },
      "sync": `
function(doc, oldDoc) {
    function isRemoved() { return (isDelete() && oldDoc == null); }
    function isDelete()  { return (doc._deleted == true); }
    if (isRemoved()) { return; }
    var combined = [];
    combined.push(doc.owner);
    if (doc.channels != null) {
        combined = combined.concat(doc.channels);
    }
    channel(combined);
}
`
    }
  }
}
